 "rationale": "The same open/close pair on windows and curtains: airing the room, shutting out rain or cold, closing up for the night.",
 "mixUps": "English 'draw the curtains' hides the direction; Japanese names it: kaaten o shimeru (close) or kaaten o akeru (open). Windows take the same akeru/shimeru as doors, with mado aiteru for the open state.",
 "targets": [
