   "noun": "mado",
   "particle": "o",
   "verb": "akeru",
   "verbJa": "開ける",
   "verbSense": "open something (a door, a box, your eyes)",
   "englishVerb": "open",
   "trap": "Not mado ga akete iru for 'the window's open': that is mado ga aiteru, or mado ga akete aru if someone left it open on purpose. akeru needs someone doing the opening (mado akete ii?).",
   "partners": [
    "doa (door)",
    "kaaten (curtains)",
    "reizouko (fridge)"
   ],
   "flags": [],
   "use": "Usually an offer or a question: mado akete ii? (mind if I open the window?), mado akeyou ka. Casual speech drops o; a window that is open is mado aiteru.",
   "notes": "In a car, mado akete just means put the window down.",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "atsui ne, mado akete ii?",
    "ja": "暑いね、窓開けていい？",
    "english": "It's hot, mind if I open the window?"
   },
   "examplePolite": {
    "romaji": "atsui desu ne, mado o akete mo ii desu ka?",
    "ja": "暑いですね、窓を開けてもいいですか？",
    "english": "It's hot, isn't it? May I open the window?"
   }
  },
